  "isolated": 1925,
  "nameOrigin": "From the Greek neos, 'new', and didymos, 'twin': the new twin separated from 'didymium'.",
  "source": "pubchem",
  "note": "CIAAW gives 1841 and Mosander, meaning the discovery of 'didymium', the mixture from which Auer separated it. Los Alamos dates the first fairly pure metal to 1925 without naming who made it.",
